    "rerun-widgets": {
      "snapshot_id": "split-e1-v1-dev-rerun-widgets",
      "hits": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "e1d-rn-1640-rerun-widgets",
          "source_id": "docs:content/develop/quick-references/release-notes/2026.md",
          "excerpt": "Bug fix: Widgets after [`st.rerun`](/develop/api-reference/execution-flow/st.rerun) keep the values the user selected, instead of resetting to their defaults ([#16762](https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/pull/16762), [#3533](https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/issues/3533))",
          "source_url": "https://docs.streamlit.io/develop/quick-reference/release-notes/2026",
          "source_type": "release_note",
          "source_commit": "695e6ce2fb1b23afc6df66b40420ab0013ad72fd",
          "applicable_versions": [
            "1.64.0"
          ],
          "source_span": "docs:content/develop/quick-references/release-notes/2026.md; Unicode codepoints [3241,3521)"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "e1d-widget-order-of-operations",
          "source_id": "docs:content/develop/concepts/architecture/widget-behavior.md",
          "excerpt": "When a user interacts with a widget, the widget is updated and triggers a rerun in the following order:\n\n1. The widget value in `st.session_state` is updated.\n2. The callback function (if any) is executed.\n3. The page reruns with the widget command returning its new value.\n\nIf the callback function displays anything on the screen, that content will appear above the rest of the page. A callback function runs as a _prefix_ to the script run. Consequently, that means anything written via a callback function will disappear as soon as the user performs their next action. Widget commands should generally not be called within a callback function.\n\n<Note>\n\nIf a callback function is passed any args or kwargs, those arguments will be established when the widget command is called, not later when the user interacts with the widget. In particular, if you want to use a widget's value in its own callback function, you can't pass that value to the callback function via the `args` parameter; you must assign a key to the widget and look up its value using `st.session_state` _within the callback function_.",
          "source_url": "https://docs.streamlit.io/develop/concepts/architecture/widget-behavior",
          "source_type": "doc",
          "source_commit": "695e6ce2fb1b23afc6df66b40420ab0013ad72fd",
          "applicable_versions": [],
          "source_span": "docs:content/develop/concepts/architecture/widget-behavior.md; Unicode codepoints [8261,9365)"
        }
      ]
    },
